---
description: 
globs: 
alwaysApply: true
---
- prefer functional coding style over adding classes
- functions should have most simple input arguments and should return most simple result
- functions should be as pure as its possible
- avoid global state
- avoid comments and docstrings if possible. Code should be an documentation itself
- minimize setup of data structures. Make setup part of code as explicit and modifiable as possible
- project uses `uv` for managing packages, so when running an app use `uv run ...`, when installing package use `uv add ...` and so on
- use builtin bash commands or git if possible, rather than reinventing some known feature
- if possible to to implement builtin python types: list not typing.List, dict not typing.Dict, | not typing.Union, etc.